KSP STAFF MANAGEMENT, BARCODE & ATTENDANCE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
ROLE
Act as a senior full-stack software architect, UI/UX designer, Firebase engineer, security engineer, and production-level React developer.
You are working inside an existing GitHub repository through the Antigravity IDE.
Your task is to design and implement a complete, production-ready Staff Management and Barcode Attendance Management System.
Do not create a superficial demo or mockup.
The system must be functional, responsive, secure, maintainable, and ready to deploy.
Use the existing GitHub repository as the source codebase and inspect the existing project structure before making changes.
Do not unnecessarily replace existing working functionality.
________________________________________
1. CORE OBJECTIVE
Build a Staff Management system in which every staff member automatically receives:
1.	A unique Staff Code.
2.	A unique Staff ID.
3.	A generated Code 128 barcode.
4.	A ready-to-download Independent staff bar code in png to be added on cards.
5.	A complete staff profile.
6.	Attendance tracking through barcode scanning.
7.	Daily work-session tracking.
8.	Total hours worked calculation.
9.	Attendance frequency/rating.
10.	Attendance history and reports.
The system must allow an Android smartphone camera to scan the barcode directly through the web application.
A separate dedicated barcode scanner application should NOT be required.
However, the architecture should also support conventional USB/Bluetooth barcode scanners that behave like keyboard input.
________________________________________
2. TECHNOLOGY
Use the existing project technology where possible.
Preferred stack:
•	React
•	JavaScript or TypeScript, following the existing repository
•	Tailwind CSS
•	Firebase Authentication
•	Firebase Firestore
•	Firebase Storage only if the existing project already uses it or if staff photographs require it
•	Firebase Security Rules
•	GitHub for source control
•	Browser camera APIs / a reliable barcode scanning library for Code 128 scanning
•	JsBarcode or an equivalent reliable barcode-generation library for generating Code 128 barcodes
•	Lucide React icons where icons are required
•	Responsive mobile-first UI
Do not introduce unnecessary backend infrastructure.
Use Firebase as the backend unless the existing architecture requires otherwise.
________________________________________
3. STAFF CODE FORMAT
Every staff member must automatically receive a Staff Code using this exact format:
KSP-XXX-XXX-XXXX
Example:
KSP-137-052-1025
The system must generate this automatically.
The Staff Code must be human-readable.
The barcode should encode the complete Staff Code.
Use Code 128 for the barcode.
________________________________________
4. FIRST THREE DIGITS
The first three digits represent:
XXX
Digit 1 = Nationality
•	1 = Rwandan
•	2 = Foreigner
Digit 2 = Department
•	1 = Executive
•	2 = Management
•	3 = Trainer
•	4 = Other
Digit 3 = Gender
•	7 = Female
•	8 = Male
Example:
137
means:
•	1 = Rwandan
•	3 = Trainer
•	7 = Female
________________________________________
5. SECOND THREE DIGITS
The second three digits follow this structure:
XXC
The first two digits represent education level.
Education codes:
•	00 = Bachelor's Degree
•	01 = A2 [Highschool]
•	02 = A1 
•	05 = Master's Degree
•	10 = PhD
The third digit represents number of certificates:
•	0 = 0 certificates
•	1 = 1–5 certificates
•	2 = 6–10 certificates
•	3 = 11 or more certificates
Examples:
000 = Bachelor's + 0 certificates
051 = Master's + 1–5 certificates
052 = Master's + 6–10 certificates
103 = PhD + 11+ certificates
________________________________________
6. FINAL FOUR DIGITS
The final four digits follow:
BXXX
The first digit represents branch:
•	1 = Kigali
•	2 = Kayonza
•	3 = Elsewhere
The final three digits represent the employee's sequential number.
Examples:
1001 = Kigali + Employee 001
2017 = Kayonza + Employee 017
3025 = Elsewhere + Employee 025
The system must automatically determine the next available employee number.
Do not create duplicate Staff Codes.
The employee sequence must be unique according to the required numbering rules.
Use Firestore transactions where necessary to prevent duplicate employee numbers when multiple administrators create staff simultaneously.
________________________________________
7. IMPORTANT DATABASE DESIGN RULE
DO NOT use the KSP Staff Code as the immutable database primary key.
Every employee must have a permanent internal unique identifier, preferably a Firebase-generated document ID or UUID.
Example:
Internal ID:
abc123xyz
Staff Code:
KSP-137-052-1025
The internal ID must remain unchanged even if the employee's department, gender, education, nationality, branch, or certificate range changes.
The KSP Staff Code should be treated as the employee's human-readable identification code.
If information that contributes to the Staff Code changes, provide a controlled mechanism to regenerate/reissue the Staff Code while preserving the employee's permanent internal identity and historical records.
Never lose historical attendance data because a Staff Code changes.
________________________________________
8. STAFF CREATION
Create a complete Staff Creation form.
Fields should include:
•	First Name
•	Middle Name
•	Last Name
•	Gender
•	Nationality
•	Department
•	Branch
•	Education Level
•	Number/Range of Certificates
•	Position/Job Title
•	Phone Number
•	Email
•	Date Joined
•	Employment Status
•	Optional emergency/contact information where appropriate
•	Notes
The system should automatically generate:
•	Internal Staff ID
•	Staff Code
•	Barcode
The administrator must NOT manually type the Staff Code.
The system generates it.
________________________________________
9. STAFF BAR CODE
Create a professional ready – to – download Barcode in PDF of PNG.
The barcode must be clearly readable by smartphone cameras and standard barcode scanners.
Use a high-contrast Code 128 barcode.
Provide:
•	Download/Generate PDF if supported by the project architecture
•	Regenerate Barcode
Do not encode private personal information directly into the barcode.
The barcode should primarily encode:
KSP-XXX-XXX-XXXX
The ERP retrieves staff information from Firebase after the code is scanned.
________________________________________
10. BARCODE SCANNING
Implement barcode scanning directly inside the web application.
The application must be able to use an Android smartphone camera.
The user should open the relevant scanning page.
The browser requests camera permission.
The camera detects the Code 128 barcode.
The application extracts the Staff Code.
Example:
KSP-137-052-1025
The system then finds the corresponding staff member in Firestore.
The scanner must support continuous scanning without requiring the user to reload the page after every scan.
Provide:
•	Start scanner
•	Stop scanner
•	Camera selection where supported
•	Flashlight/torch support where browser/device APIs permit
•	Manual Staff Code entry as a fallback
•	Clear scan result
•	Scan success feedback
•	Scan error feedback
The system should prevent duplicate rapid scans caused by the same barcode remaining in front of the camera.
Implement a configurable scan cooldown/debounce mechanism.
________________________________________
11. ATTENDANCE SCANNER PAGE
Create a dedicated:
ATTENDANCE SCANNER
page.
This page has one primary purpose:
Record staff attendance.
When a barcode is scanned on this page, DO NOT simply display the profile.
The system must determine whether the employee should be clocked IN or OUT.
________________________________________
12. ODD/EVEN SCAN ATTENDANCE LOGIC
Use alternating attendance sessions.
For each staff member and each working day:
1st scan = CLOCK IN
2nd scan = CLOCK OUT
3rd scan = CLOCK IN
4th scan = CLOCK OUT
5th scan = CLOCK IN
6th scan = CLOCK OUT
Continue this alternating pattern throughout the day.
Example:
08:02 → IN
12:00 → OUT
13:00 → IN
17:10 → OUT
The system must calculate each session duration.
Example:
08:02–12:00 = 3h 58m
13:00–17:10 = 4h 10m
Total = 8h 08m
________________________________________
13. OPEN SESSION PROTECTION
If an employee has an open IN session, the next valid scan should normally close that session.
Example:
IN 08:00
OUT 17:00
If the employee scans again:
IN 18:00
If the employee scans again:
OUT 19:00
The system must maintain all sessions separately.
If the working day ends with an open session, clearly mark it as:
OPEN SESSION
and allow an authorized administrator/manager to correct it.
Do not silently fabricate a departure time.
________________________________________
14. ATTENDANCE SCANNER FEEDBACK
After scanning, show a large visual confirmation.
For IN:
CLOCKED IN
Staff Name
Staff Photo (Direct profile image link | directly displayed)
Staff Code
Arrival Time
Current Total Hours
For OUT:
CLOCKED OUT
Staff Name
Staff Photo (Direct profile image link | directly displayed)
Staff Code
Departure Time
Current Session Duration
Total Hours Worked Today
Use strong visual feedback and optional sound feedback.
The scanner page should automatically return to the scanning state after a short configurable period.
