•	Late arrivals
•	Attendance percentage
•	Attendance rating out of 10
Where appropriate, provide authorized managers/administrators with historical attendance information.
Do not expose sensitive information to users who do not have permission.
________________________________________
17. ATTENDANCE RATING
Separate attendance from performance.
Calculate:
Attendance Percentage:
Days Present / Expected Working Days × 100
Then calculate an Attendance Rating:
Attendance Percentage / 10
Example:
92% attendance
= 9.2 / 10
Do not call this a job performance score.
Label it:
ATTENDANCE RATING
A separate PERFORMANCE RATING should be implemented independently if required.
Managers should be able to assign performance ratings according to their permissions.
________________________________________
18. JOB/PERFORMANCE RATING
Create a separate performance rating system.
Rating:
0–10
Possible categories:
•	Attendance
•	Punctuality
•	Productivity
•	Professionalism
•	Quality of Work
•	Teamwork
Allow authorized managers to enter ratings.
Calculate an overall performance rating.
Do not automatically equate attendance with job performance.
Display separately:
Attendance Rating: 9.2/10
Performance Rating: 8.7/10
Overall Rating: 8.9/10
If management has not entered a performance rating, show:
Not Rated
instead of inventing one.
________________________________________
19. WORKING HOURS
Calculate working hours from actual attendance sessions.
Do not calculate hours simply from:
First Arrival → Final Departure
because employees may leave and return multiple times.
Correct calculation:
Session 1:
IN → OUT
Session 2:
IN → OUT
Session 3:
IN → OUT
Total:
Session 1 + Session 2 + Session 3
Store durations in minutes in the database for reliable calculations.
Display them in human-readable format:
8h 42m
________________________________________
20. ATTENDANCE HISTORY
Every scan must create an auditable record.
Store:
•	Staff internal ID
•	Staff Code
•	Timestamp
•	Date
•	Scan type
•	IN/OUT status
•	Device/browser information where appropriate
•	User/operator if applicable
•	Location only if explicitly implemented and authorized
•	Attendance record ID
Do not overwrite historical scans.
Attendance history must remain auditable.
