27. BARCODE GENERATION
Generate Code 128 barcodes from Staff Codes.
Example:
KSP-137-052-1025
The generated barcode should:
•	Have sufficient quiet zone
•	Have sufficient width/height
•	Have high contrast
•	Include human-readable Staff Code underneath
•	Be printable
•	Remain scannable when printed on an ID card
Do not generate QR codes unless specifically required as an additional feature.
The primary identification barcode is Code 128.
________________________________________
28. STAFF ID GENERATION
When creating a staff member:
1.	Validate form.
2.	Determine classification digits.
3.	Determine education/certificate digits.
4.	Determine branch digit.
5.	Generate sequential employee number.
6.	Construct Staff Code.
7.	Verify uniqueness.
8.	Save staff record.
9.	Generate barcode.
10.	Make Staff ID card available for printing.
Example:
KSP-137-052-1025
