35. IMPORTANT BEHAVIORAL DISTINCTION
There are two different scanning contexts.
ATTENDANCE SCANNER
Barcode scan:
Staff Identification
↓
Check today's attendance
↓
If no open session:
CLOCK IN
↓
If open session exists:
CLOCK OUT
↓
Update total working hours
GENERAL STAFF SCANNER
Barcode scan:
Staff Identification
↓
Retrieve Staff Profile
↓
Display full authorized staff information
↓
DO NOT modify attendance
The same barcode must therefore have context-sensitive behavior depending on which module initiated the scan.
________________________________________
36. FUTURE EXTENSIBILITY
Architect the system so that the same Staff ID can later be used for:
•	Access control
•	Equipment assignment
•	Payroll
•	Leave management
•	Training records
•	Performance management
•	Task assignment
•	Asset management
•	Visitor/staff identification
•	Staff directory
Do not tightly couple barcode scanning exclusively to attendance.
The barcode is the staff identification mechanism.
Attendance is one application of that identification mechanism.
