38. DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLE
Do not simply generate code that looks correct.
Think through the actual business workflow.
The system will be used by real staff members and administrators.
Prioritize:
•	Data integrity
•	Security
•	Accurate time calculations
•	Reliable barcode scanning
•	Prevention of duplicate records
•	Auditability
•	Usability
•	Maintainability
•	Mobile performance
•	Firebase scalability
Before implementing each major feature, inspect how it fits into the existing application.
If an existing feature can be reused, extend it instead of duplicating it.
If a requirement is ambiguous, inspect the existing application architecture and choose the safest production-ready implementation rather than creating a temporary workaround.
Finally, run the application, test the complete user journey from:
CREATE STAFF
→ GENERATE STAFF CODE
→ GENERATE BARCODE
→ PRINT STAFF ID
→ SCAN STAFF ID
→ CLOCK IN
→ CLOCK OUT
→ CALCULATE HOURS
→ VIEW STAFF PROFILE
→ VIEW ATTENDANCE HISTORY
→ GENERATE REPORT
and fix all errors encountered before declaring the implementation complete.

